{
  "note": "What each room's own picture already paints, measured off tools/art/rooms_*.py in 1x logical pixels from the room's top-left. It exists so tools/selftest/slots.ts can prove that a designed decor slot does not stand a sprite on top of the building. \"standing\": true marks a fixture that occupies FLOOR — a desk, a counter, the pool itself — which is what a floor slot must keep clear of; everything else is on the wall, and furniture standing in front of it is the arrangement rather than a clash. Update it in the same commit as any change to a room routine. \"behind\": true marks a fixture the room paints on its own front layer (rooms/<id>_front.png, BL-035) — somebody may stand on that floor line and be hidden from the waist down by it, which is what a desk is for. Such a fixture also carries \"paint\": the alpha bounds of what that layer actually draws, measured off the file. The two differ and both are needed: x0..y1 is the furniture's body, which is what decor must not stand on, while \"paint\" adds the outline, the bell and ledger on the counter top and the skirt that hides a character's feet — which is what the front layer may cover and nothing more.",
